{"v":15,"id":"e01","kid":"emma","title":"The Lion and the Mouse","zh":"狮子和老鼠","level":"A2","genre":"寓言故事","src":"aesop","sum":"伊索寓言改写。狮子放走了吵醒它的小老鼠；后来狮子被猎人的网困住，小老鼠咬断绳子救了它。善意从不白费。","words":304,"paras":[{"t":"One hot afternoon, a big lion was sleeping under a tree in the forest. A little mouse came out of its hole to look for food. It did not see the lion, and it ran right across his nose.","w":[[0,3,"one",-1],[4,7,"hot",-1],[8,17,"afternoon",-1],[19,20,"a",-1],[21,24,"big",-1],[25,29,"lion",-1],[30,33,"was",-1],[34,42,"sleeping",-1],[43,48,"under",-1],[49,50,"a",-1],[51,55,"tree",-1],[56,58,"in",-1],[59,62,"the",-1],[63,69,"forest",-1],[71,72,"a",-1],[73,79,"little",-1],[80,85,"mouse",-1],[86,90,"came",-1],[91,94,"out",-1],[95,97,"of",-1],[98,101,"its",-1],[102,106,"hole",-1],[107,109,"to",-1],[110,114,"look",0],[115,118,"for",0],[119,123,"food",-1],[125,127,"it",-1],[128,131,"did",-1],[132,135,"not",-1],[136,139,"see",-1],[140,143,"the",-1],[144,148,"lion",-1],[150,153,"and",-1],[154,156,"it",-1],[157,160,"ran",-1],[161,166,"right",-1],[167,173,"across",-1],[174,177,"his",-1],[178,182,"nose",-1]]},{"t":"The lion woke up with a loud roar. He caught the mouse under his huge paw. \"How dare you wake me up?\" he shouted. \"Now I am going to eat you!\"","w":[[0,3,"the",-1],[4,8,"lion",-1],[9,13,"woke",1],[14,16,"up",1],[17,21,"with",-1],[22,23,"a",-1],[24,28,"loud",-1],[29,33,"roar",-1],[35,37,"he",-1],[38,44,"caught",-1],[45,48,"the",-1],[49,54,"mouse",-1],[55,60,"under",-1],[61,64,"his",-1],[65,69,"huge",-1],[70,73,"paw",-1],[76,79,"how",2],[80,84,"dare",2],[85,88,"you",2],[89,93,"wake",-1],[94,96,"me",-1],[97,99,"up",-1],[102,104,"he",-1],[105,112,"shouted",-1],[115,118,"now",-1],[119,120,"i",-1],[121,123,"am",-1],[124,129,"going",-1],[130,132,"to",-1],[133,136,"eat",-1],[137,140,"you",-1]]},{"t":"The mouse was shaking with fear. \"Please let me go,\" it cried. \"I am too small to be a good meal for you. If you set me free, one day I will help you.\"","w":[[0,3,"the",-1],[4,9,"mouse",-1],[10,13,"was",-1],[14,21,"shaking",-1],[22,26,"with",-1],[27,31,"fear",-1],[34,40,"please",-1],[41,44,"let",3],[45,47,"me",3],[48,50,"go",3],[53,55,"it",-1],[56,61,"cried",-1],[64,65,"i",-1],[66,68,"am",-1],[69,72,"too",-1],[73,78,"small",-1],[79,81,"to",-1],[82,84,"be",-1],[85,86,"a",-1],[87,91,"good",-1],[92,96,"meal",-1],[97,100,"for",-1],[101,104,"you",-1],[106,108,"if",-1],[109,112,"you",-1],[113,116,"set",5],[117,119,"me",5],[120,124,"free",5],[126,129,"one",6],[130,133,"day",6],[134,135,"i",-1],[136,140,"will",-1],[141,145,"help",-1],[146,149,"you",-1]]},{"t":"The lion laughed. \"How can a tiny mouse like you ever help a great lion like me?\" But he thought the mouse was funny, and he was not very hungry. So he lifted his paw and let the mouse go.","w":[[0,3,"the",-1],[4,8,"lion",-1],[9,16,"laughed",-1],[19,22,"how",-1],[23,26,"can",-1],[27,28,"a",-1],[29,33,"tiny",-1],[34,39,"mouse",-1],[40,44,"like",-1],[45,48,"you",-1],[49,53,"ever",-1],[54,58,"help",-1],[59,60,"a",-1],[61,66,"great",-1],[67,71,"lion",-1],[72,76,"like",-1],[77,79,"me",-1],[82,85,"but",-1],[86,88,"he",-1],[89,96,"thought",-1],[97,100,"the",-1],[101,106,"mouse",-1],[107,110,"was",-1],[111,116,"funny",-1],[118,121,"and",-1],[122,124,"he",-1],[125,128,"was",-1],[129,132,"not",-1],[133,137,"very",-1],[138,144,"hungry",-1],[146,148,"so",-1],[149,151,"he",-1],[152,158,"lifted",-1],[159,162,"his",-1],[163,166,"paw",-1],[167,170,"and",-1],[171,174,"let",4],[175,178,"the",4],[179,184,"mouse",4],[185,187,"go",4]]},{"t":"A few days later, some hunters came into the forest. They wanted to catch the lion and take him to the king. They put a strong net on the ground and hid it under some leaves. When the lion walked by, he stepped into the trap. The net closed around him. He pulled and bit and rolled, but he could not get out. He roared angrily, and the sound filled the whole forest.","w":[[0,1,"a",7],[2,5,"few",7],[6,10,"days",7],[11,16,"later",7],[18,22,"some",-1],[23,30,"hunters",-1